From: Realme X2 Pro Linux port <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: use the standard DHCP config and restore NM ownership

Read the standard /etc/unudhcpd.conf address pair so the generated
NetworkManager profile and unudhcpd service cannot diverge. Also restore
NetworkManager ownership of the NCM interface before creating the profile:
a board migration may have left usb0 marked unmanaged at runtime.
---
diff --git a/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-developer-mode.sh b/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-developer-mode.sh
index 995cbc7..745d8e7 100644
--- a/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-developer-mode.sh
+++ b/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-developer-mode.sh
@@ -6,8 +6,13 @@
 CONFIGFS="/sys/kernel/config/usb_gadget"
 IFACE=$(cat "$CONFIGFS"/usb-signaller-developer/functions/ncm.*/ifname 2>/dev/null)
 IFACE=${IFACE:-"usb0"}
-IP_ADDRESS_SERVER=172.16.42.1
-IP_ADDRESS_CLIENT=172.16.42.2
+# A legacy board gadget may have left this interface unmanaged at runtime.
+# usb-signaller is the owner of the interface while this mode is active.
+nmcli device set "$IFACE" managed yes
+# The file unudhcpd's systemd unit takes its addresses from
+[ -r /etc/unudhcpd.conf ] && . /etc/unudhcpd.conf
+IP_ADDRESS_SERVER=${UNUDHCPD_SERVER:-172.16.42.1}
+IP_ADDRESS_CLIENT=${UNUDHCPD_CLIENT:-172.16.42.2}
 CONNECTION_NAME=$(cat "$CONFIGFS"/usb-signaller-developer/configs/*/strings/0x409/configuration 2>/dev/null)
 CONNECTION_NAME=${CONNECTION_NAME:-"Developer Mode"}
 
diff --git a/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-tethering-mode.sh b/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-tethering-mode.sh
index 16560ba..0d12158 100644
--- a/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-tethering-mode.sh
+++ b/distro/scripts/usb-signaller-tethering-mode.sh
@@ -6,6 +6,9 @@
 CONFIGFS="/sys/kernel/config/usb_gadget"
 IFACE=$(cat "$CONFIGFS"/usb-signaller-tethering/functions/ncm.*/ifname 2>/dev/null)
 IFACE=${IFACE:-"usb0"}
+# A legacy board gadget may have left this interface unmanaged at runtime.
+# usb-signaller is the owner of the interface while this mode is active.
+nmcli device set "$IFACE" managed yes
 CONNECTION_NAME=$(cat "$CONFIGFS"/usb-signaller-tethering/configs/*/strings/0x409/configuration 2>/dev/null)
 CONNECTION_NAME=${CONNECTION_NAME:-"Tethering Mode"}
 
